    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "text": "Stop 2: Punctuation"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "markdown": "**Capital letters** begin sentences and names. A **comma** separates the things in a list. **Speech marks** go round the exact words someone says. An **apostrophe** shows that letters are missing, or that something belongs to someone."
  },
