  {
   "type": "heading",
   "text": "Stop 4: Building words and meanings"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "markdown": "A **prefix** goes at the start of a word and changes its meaning, like un in unhappy. A **suffix** goes at the end, like ful in careful.\n\nClap the beats in a word. Un-hap-py has 3 beats, also called syllables."
  },
  {
   "type": "explainer",
   "title": "Building new words",
   "scenes": [
    {
     "caption": "Start with happy.",
     "items": [
      {
       "id": "a",
       "emoji": "😊",
       "x": 50,
       "y": 55,
       "size": 3,
       "anim": "none",
       "label": "happy"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "caption": "Add the prefix un. It means not.",
     "items": [
      {
       "id": "a",
       "emoji": "😊",
       "x": 65,
       "y": 55,
       "size": 3,
       "anim": "none",
       "label": "happy"
      },
      {
       "id": "p",
       "emoji": "🔹",
       "x": 30,
       "y": 55,
       "size": 3,
       "anim": "grow",
       "label": "un"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "caption": "Unhappy means not happy.",
     "items": [
      {
       "id": "a",
       "emoji": "😞",
       "x": 50,
       "y": 55,
       "size": 3,
       "anim": "none",
       "label": "unhappy"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
